         <div type="bio">
            <p>American novelist, best known for his <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Jurgen: A Comedy of Justice</name> (New York: Robert M. McBride, 1919), whose eponymous character’s racy adventures brought the book to the attention of the New York Society for the Suppression of Vice and its secretary, <name type="person" key="sumn76">John S. Sumner</name>. Banned, the book became notoriously famous and, after being acquitted in its 1922 obscenity trial, became a best-seller. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
